        "content": "Pure classification logic (`crm`/`warehouse`/`synthetic` bucketing) sitting inside an async DB-touching module. It's currently untestable in isolation because it calls `listSources()` directly rather than accepting data — that's a **testability gap**, not just a coverage gap.\n\n**Gap:** no unit tests exercise the classification for each `SourceKind`; no test covers empty source list; no test covers duplicate kinds within a side.\n\nSuggested minimal refactor to make this testable without a DB:\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.ts\nexport function classifySourcesBySide(all: Source[]) {\n  return {\n    crm: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"salesforce\" || s.kind === \"hubspot\").length,\n    warehouse: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"databricks\" || s.kind === \"snowflake\").length,\n    synthetic: all.filter((s) => s.kind === \"synthetic\").length,\n  };\n}\nexport async function countSourcesBySide() {\n  return classifySourcesBySide(await listSources());\n}\n```\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { classifySourcesBySide } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport type { Source } from \"@/types/source\";\n\nconst mk = (kind: Source[\"kind\"], id: string): Source => ({\n  id, name: id, kind, config: { objects: [\"Account\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n});\n\ndescribe(\"classifySourcesBySide\", () => {\n  it(\"returns zero counts for an empty list\", () => {\n    expect(classifySourcesBySide([])).toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"buckets salesforce and hubspot as crm\", () => {\n    const result = classifySourcesBySide([mk(\"salesforce\", \"1\"), mk(\"hubspot\", \"2\")]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"buckets databricks and snowflake as warehouse\", () => {\n    const result = classifySourcesBySide([mk(\"databricks\", \"1\"), mk(\"snowflake\", \"2\")]);\n    expect(result).toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 2, synthetic: 0 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"buckets synthetic separately\", () => {\n    expect(classifySourcesBySide([mk(\"synthetic\", \"1\")])).toEqual({ crm: 0, warehouse: 0, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"counts a mixed list correctly\", () => {\n    const all = [mk(\"salesforce\", \"1\"), mk(\"databricks\", \"2\"), mk(\"synthetic\", \"3\"), mk(\"hubspot\", \"4\")];\n    expect(classifySourcesBySide(all)).toEqual({ crm: 2, warehouse: 1, synthetic: 1 });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**Integration gap:** `listSources()` itself (DB query + `sourceSchema.parse` + ordering) has no test. It needs either an integration test against a real/test Postgres, or the query layer needs to be injectable. Skeleton for the integration version:\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/sources.integration.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n// requires a test DATABASE_URL and drizzle-kit migrate against a disposable schema\ndescribe(\"listSources (integration)\", () => {\n  beforeEach(async () => { /* truncate sources table */ });\n\n  it(\"returns rows ordered by createdAt ascending\", async () => { /* seed 3 rows out of order, assert order */ });\n  it(\"parses stored config through sourceSchema and rejects malformed rows\", async () => { /* insert a row with missing config.objects, assert throws */ });\n  it(\"returns an empty array when no sources are configured\", async () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "4. `types/source.ts` — Zod schemas, 0% covered",
        "content": "Validation boundaries are exactly where regressions hide silently (a schema loosened by accident lets bad data into `sources`).\n\n```ts\n// types/source.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { createSourceSchema, sourceConfigSchema, sourceKindSchema } from \"@/types/source\";\n\ndescribe(\"sourceKindSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts each known kind\", () => {\n    for (const k of [\"salesforce\", \"hubspot\", \"databricks\", \"snowflake\", \"synthetic\"]) {\n      expect(sourceKindSchema.parse(k)).toBe(k);\n    }\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an unknown kind\", () => {\n    expect(() => sourceKindSchema.parse(\"bigquery\")).toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"sourceConfigSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"requires at least one object\", () => {\n    expect(() => sourceConfigSchema.parse({ objects: [] })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"allows filter to be omitted\", () => {\n    expect(sourceConfigSchema.parse({ objects: [\"Account\"] }).filter).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"createSourceSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects a name over 80 chars\", () => {\n    const name = \"a\".repeat(81);\n    expect(() => createSourceSchema.parse({ name, kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] } })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an empty name\", () => {\n    expect(() => createSourceSchema.parse({ name: \"\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] } })).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"accepts a minimal valid payload\", () => {\n    expect(() =>\n      createSourceSchema.parse({ name: \"Prod SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\", config: { objects: [\"Account\"] } }),\n    ).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n```\n\nAlso untested: `SOURCE_KIND_LABEL` / `SOURCE_KIND_SIDE` completeness — a new `SourceKind` added to the enum without a matching label/side entry would only fail at runtime (`undefined` rendered in the table). Worth a static-completeness test:\n\n```ts\nit(\"has a label and a side for every SourceKind\", () => {\n  for (const kind of sourceKindSchema.options) {\n    expect(SOURCE_KIND_LABEL[kind]).toBeDefined();\n    expect(SOURCE_KIND_SIDE[kind]).toBeDefined();\n  }\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "5. `lib/server/auth.ts` — `requireReviewer` / `getReviewer`, 0% covered",
        "content": "Security-relevant boundary: this is the function that guarantees `audit_log.actor` is never client-supplied. No test currently proves the throw path fires, or that `getReviewer` returns `null` instead of throwing when signed out.\n\n**Gaps:** unauthenticated → `requireReviewer` throws; unauthenticated → `getReviewer` returns `null` (not throw); authenticated → `label` is derived via `reviewerLabel` (not duplicated logic).\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/auth.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { requireReviewer, getReviewer } from \"@/lib/server/auth\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@clerk/nextjs/server\", () => ({\n  auth: vi.fn(),\n  currentUser: vi.fn(),\n}));\nimport { auth, currentUser } from \"@clerk/nextjs/server\";\n\ndescribe(\"requireReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"throws when there is no authenticated session\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null } as never);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow(/No authenticated reviewer/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when isAuthenticated is true but userId is missing (matcher/handler disagreement)\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: null } as never);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).rejects.toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns userId and a derived label when authenticated\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as never);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: null } as never);\n    await expect(requireReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"getReviewer\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when signed out instead of throwing\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: false, userId: null } as never);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"delegates to requireReviewer when signed in\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(auth).mockResolvedValue({ isAuthenticated: true, userId: \"uid_1\" } as never);\n    vi.mocked(currentUser).mockResolvedValue({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"a@b.com\" } } as never);\n    await expect(getReviewer()).resolves.toEqual({ userId: \"uid_1\", label: \"a@b.com\" });\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `proxy.ts` (Clerk middleware / route matcher) — 0% covered",
        "content": "This is the entire auth boundary for the app — \"Anything not named here requires a session\" — and has no test proving the public-route allowlist is exactly `/`, `/sign-in*`, `/sign-up*`, nor that everything else is protected.\n\n**Gap:** no test on `isPublicRoute` logic; the function isn't exported, which blocks testing it directly (testability gap).\n\nSuggested: export `isPublicRoute` for testing, or test indirectly via the `matcher` regex.\n\n```ts\n// proxy.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n// requires exporting isPublicRoute from proxy.ts\nimport { isPublicRoute } from \"@/proxy\";\n\ndescribe(\"isPublicRoute\", () => {\n  it.each([\"/\", \"/sign-in\", \"/sign-in/factor-one\", \"/sign-up\", \"/sign-up/verify\"])(\n    \"treats %s as public\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute({ url: `https://x.test${path}` } as never)).toBe(true),\n  );\n\n  it.each([\"/sources\", \"/api/sources\", \"/console\", \"/sign-in-not-really\"])(\n    \"treats %s as protected\",\n    (path) => expect(isPublicRoute({ url: `https://x.test${path}` } as never)).toBe(false),\n  );\n});\n```\n\n**Integration gap:** no test that `clerkMiddleware`'s `auth.protect()` is actually invoked for a non-public route and skipped for a public one — best covered with an E2E test (Playwright) hitting `/sources` unauthenticated and asserting a redirect to sign-in.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "7. Components — 0% covered across the board",
        "content": "Every component in `components/` has zero rendering tests. Priority order by logic density:\n\n**`components/sources/source-table.tsx`** — renders derived label/side lookups per row.\n```tsx\n// components/sources/source-table.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport { SourceTable } from \"@/components/sources/source-table\";\n\nconst source = {\n  id: \"1\", name: \"Prod SFDC\", kind: \"salesforce\" as const,\n  config: { objects: [\"Account\", \"Contact\"] }, createdAt: new Date(),\n};\n\ndescribe(\"SourceTable\", () => {\n  it(\"renders an empty tbody for an empty list\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[]} />);\n    expect(screen.queryAllByRole(\"row\")).toHaveLength(1); // header only\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders the mapped kind label and side, not the raw enum value\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Salesforce\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"crm\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"joins multiple objects with a comma\", () => {\n    render(<SourceTable sources={[source]} />);\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"Account, Contact\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`components/ui/button.tsx`** — variant/size class composition, `asChild` polymorphism, disabled state.\n```tsx\n// components/ui/button.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nimport userEvent from \"@testing-library/user-event\";\nimport { Button } from \"@/components/ui/button\";\n\ndescribe(\"Button\", () => {\n  it(\"renders as a <button> by default\", () => {\n    render(<Button>Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Go\" }).tagName).toBe(\"BUTTON\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders the child element in place when asChild is set\", () => {\n    render(<Button asChild><a href=\"/x\">Go</a></Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Go\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not fire onClick when disabled\", async () => {\n    const onClick = vi.fn();\n    render(<Button disabled onClick={onClick}>Go</Button>);\n    await userEvent.click(screen.getByRole(\"button\"));\n    expect(onClick).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"merges a caller className without dropping variant classes\", () => {\n    render(<Button className=\"custom\">Go</Button>);\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\").className).toContain(\"custom\");\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"button\").className).toContain(\"bg-g-900\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`app/(console)/sources/page.tsx`** — the empty-state/table branch, currently untested at any level.\n```tsx\n// app/(console)/sources/page.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { render, screen } from \"@testing-library/react\";\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\", () => ({ listSources: vi.fn() }));\nimport { listSources } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport SourcesPage from \"@/app/(console)/sources/page\";\n\ndescribe(\"SourcesPage\", () => {\n  it(\"renders SourcesEmptyState when there are no sources\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(listSources).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"No sources yet\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n\n  it(\"renders the table and an Add source action when sources exist\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(listSources).mockResolvedValue([\n      { id: \"1\", name: \"A\", kind: \"synthetic\", config: { objects: [\"x\"] }, createdAt: new Date() },\n    ]);\n    render(await SourcesPage());\n    expect(screen.getByText(\"1 configured\")).toBeInTheDocument();\n    expect(screen.getByRole(\"link\", { name: \"Add source\" })).toBeInTheDocument();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n**`components/auth/sign-out-control.tsx`** — untested `full` prop / className merge branch (low priority, thin wrapper).\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "8. `lib/server/sources.ts` error handling — missing entirely",
        "content": "- No test for `getDb()` throwing when `DATABASE_URL` is unset (the explicit, actionable error path in `lib/db/index.ts:32`).\n- No test for `sourceSchema.parse` rejecting a row that fails validation (malformed `config` from a bad migration/manual edit) — currently this would throw an unhandled `ZodError` all the way up through `listSources` with no coverage proving *that's* the intended behavior vs. silently dropping the row.\n\n```ts\n// lib/db/index.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"getDb\", () => {\n  const original = process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n  beforeEach(() => { delete process.env.DATABASE_URL; delete (globalThis as never).canonDb; });\n  afterEach(() => { process.env.DATABASE_URL = original; });\n\n  it(\"throws an actionable error when DATABASE_URL is unset\", async () => {\n    const { getDb } = await import(\"@/lib/db\");\n    expect(() => getDb()).toThrow(/DATABASE_URL is not set/);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "9. Integration-test gaps (no scaffolding exists for any of these)",
        "content": "- **Auth → DB write path:** a review action end-to-end — signed-in reviewer resolves a conflict, `audit_log.actor` is the reviewer's stable `userId`/label, never a client string. This is the one AGENTS.md explicitly calls a hard invariant (`lib/server/auth.ts:12`), and it's currently unverified by any test.\n- **Ownership boundary:** nothing asserts web code never writes to `entities`/`matches`/`conflicts` (engine-owned tables) — worth a lint-level or migration-level guard, not just a unit test, but flagging since schema.ts documents this as load-bearing.\n- **`sources` round-trip:** create a source via the (not-yet-built) `/sources/new` handler → appears in `listSources()` → renders in `SourceTable`. No route handler exists yet for source creation, so this is a gap that will land alongside that feature, not a regression today.\n- **Middleware redirect:** unauthenticated request to a protected route redirects to sign-in; request to `/` succeeds without a session. Best done as a Playwright E2E test since `proxy.ts` is framework middleware, not a unit-testable function without refactoring.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "Priority order if you can only do a subset",
        "content": "1. `lib/reviewer-label.ts`, `lib/server/auth.ts` — small, pure-ish, and guard the audit-trail integrity invariant.\n2. `types/source.ts` schema tests — cheap, catches silent validation regressions.\n3. `lib/server/sources.ts` (after the `classifySourcesBySide` extraction) — same reasoning.\n4. `proxy.ts` `isPublicRoute` (after exporting it) — this is the entire access-control surface for an internal tool with org-chart data.\n5. Component tests, starting with `SourceTable` and the `SourcesPage` branch logic.",
        "level": 3
      }
    ],
